<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eutychius (exarch)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eutychius was the last Byzantine exarch of Ravenna, governing from the late 720s. He struggled to defend imperial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a>, at times seeking help from the popes, while the dispute over Iconoclasm divided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. When the Lombard king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aistulf">Aistulf</a> captured Ravenna in 751, the exarchate came to an end.</p></div>
